INT. ARCTIC SEAFOOD COLD STORAGE - LOADING BAY - NIGHT

Minus twenty-five. Breath fogs the air like cigar smoke. Pallets of frozen cod stacked ten feet high, shrink-wrapped, glittering with frost. A forklift sleeps beside a hanging scale. Strip lights hum.

Six figures in white parkas move through the aisle with the quiet efficiency of a crew that has done this before.

SOLEDAD RIVERA, 40s, the planner, leads, carrying a blueprint rolled in a tube. WYATT PRUITT, 30s, the driver, gnaws a toothpick and watches the door. LINH TRAN, 30s, the safecracker, drags a rolling case with a plasma cutter. IGNATIUS OKORO, 50s, the inside man, in a foreman's hard hat, jingles a ring of keys. FERN HALLORAN-BOSE, 20s, a hacker, cradles a laptop in gloved hands. BOONE DAKOTA, 40s, the muscle, carries a duffel in each fist.

SOLEDAD
(quietly)
Remember. We're out in twelve.

WYATT
Van's at the dock.

FERN
Cameras are looped.

LINH
Vault's behind the tuna. Third freezer.

IGNATIUS
That's the one with the red tag.

SOLEDAD
Boone. Door.

BOONE
(low)
On it.

He sets the duffels down and shoulders a heavy steel door, the hinge shrieking in the cold. They enter a smaller freezer. Hanging halves of beef sway. Linh crouches at a steel panel in the back wall.

LINH
Here.

She flips a switch. The plasma cutter hisses, blue-white, and begins to draw a circle on the steel. Sparks fall like snow. Fern stands guard with the laptop open, tapping.

FERN
(muttering to herself)
Come on, come on, stay dumb...

WYATT
Twelve minutes.

SOLEDAD
Eleven.

IGNATIUS
Is it always this cold?

BOONE
It's a freezer.

IGNATIUS
I meant the vault.

LINH
The vault's not cold. It's a safe room. It has a heater.

IGNATIUS
Why would it have a heater?

LINH
Because someone puts a person in it.

They all look at her. She doesn't look up. The cutter sputters.

SOLEDAD
(to the group)
Let's keep our heads. Boone, how's the watch?

BOONE
Quiet.

WYATT
(to himself)
Quiet is bad.

Fern's laptop chirps. A red banner scrolls across the screen. Her face drains.

FERN
Sol.

SOLEDAD
What?

FERN
The loop broke.

Linh kills the cutter. The silence is enormous.

SOLEDAD
How long?

FERN
Ninety seconds.

IGNATIUS
That's impossible. I set the loop.

BOONE
Somebody else did.

They freeze. Down the corridor, far off, boots on concrete. Several pairs. Unhurried.

SOLEDAD
Positions.

Wyatt slides behind a pallet. Boone pulls the door shut. Linh unsnaps a pocket. Fern closes her laptop and puts it on the floor, very gently. Ignatius backs against a hanging side of beef.

SOLEDAD (CONT'D)
(whispering)
Ignatius. Who knew about this?

IGNATIUS
Just us.

SOLEDAD
Just us.

She stares at him. Slowly, his hand goes to his hard hat. He removes it, as if to scratch his head, and the strip light catches a small black earpiece in his ear.

LINH
(very quietly)
Oh, Ignatius.

The freezer door swings open on its own. Beyond it, only the dark corridor and the sound of boots, closer.

FERN
(under her breath)
It's a trap.

SOLEDAD
Of course it's a trap, Fern. It's always a trap.

Boone raises a fist. Wyatt cocks a pistol. Linh lifts the cutter like a lance. The boots stop outside, and the frost between them seems to hold its breath.
